      "totalDuration": "5 yrs 8 mos",
      "description": "As a member of the Optimizing Translator team, I was responsible for:\n* Adding support for new OS and language features (examples would be thunk support for C++ object model, cmpswp, value preserving pointers, bounds checking, large pack decimal support and many more).\n* Added local optimizations to improve addressability expressions.\n* Improvements to algorithms for layout of automatic, static, and constant storage.\n* Involved in transition from a compilation unit level \"binding vector\" addressing model to a program level \"binding vector\" addressing model to improve call performance between compilation units.\n* Designed and implemented an automatic algorithm to improve argument passing within a compilation unit and then later designed a link-time algorithm to improve argument passing for calls outside the compilation unit.\n* Compile-time and run-time performance analysis and improvements.\n* Back up and later primary focal point for support of the Optimizing Translator for both internal and external customers.\n* For Java, I implemented Class Hierarchy Analysis and Rapid Runtime Analysis algorithms to support method devirtualization and stack allocation of objects.\n* Register Assignment improvements including more aggressive Rematerialization to lower spill cost.",
